MedSync
=======

Portions of services/laboratory-service are derived from smkazi/HaematologyIS
(https://github.com/smkazi/HaematologyIS), a Python hematology Laboratory
Information System by the same author.

Specifically, the following were ported to Java:

  services/laboratory-service/src/main/java/com/hms/laboratory/device/astm/
      AstmParser.java, AstmRecordParser.java, AstmFrames.java,
      HistogramExtractor.java
        <- parsers/astm_parser.py

  services/laboratory-service/src/main/java/com/hms/laboratory/device/kdps/
      KdpsParser.java
        <- parsers/kdps_parser.py

  The reference-range flagging rule in
  services/laboratory-service/src/main/java/com/hms/laboratory/service/
      ReferenceRangeService.java
        <- models/reference_ranges.py (range_flag / get_flag)

The test fixtures in
services/laboratory-service/src/test/resources/fixtures/ are the analyzer frames
captured from a Sysmex RX-21/XP-100 used by that project's own test suite.

Two deliberate departures from the source are documented in the ported classes:
reference-range flagging moved out of the parser into a service, because the
ranges are lab-configurable and live in the database; and K-DPS header detection
now tolerates a leading STX byte, matching the header parser's own documented
tolerance.
